
=== 1. CopyTagsToData({'session_start_datetime': 'session_start'})(experiment)
keys(): (('subject_id', 'session_start_datetime', 'experiment_index'), ('experiment_start_timestamp', 'task_id', 'session_start'))
output_schema(): (Schema({'subject_id': str, 'session_start_datetime': datetime, 'experiment_index': int}), Schema({'experiment_start_timestamp': int, 'task_id': str, 'session_start': datetime}))
as_table() columns: ['subject_id', 'session_start_datetime', 'experiment_index', 'experiment_start_timestamp', 'task_id', 'session_start']
as_table(all_info) source cols: ['_source_experiment_start_timestamp', '_source_task_id', '_source_session_start']
first iter_data(): {'subject_id': 'm1', 'session_start_datetime': datetime.datetime(2026, 1, 5, 9, 0, tzinfo=<UTC>), 'experiment_index': 0} | {'experiment_start_timestamp': 1767603660000000, 'task_id': 'fv', 'session_start': datetime.datetime(2026, 1, 5, 9, 0, tzinfo=<UTC>)}
prediction matches static_process: True
... also with columns={'source': True} (no stream lists _source_ columns): True
validation {'session_start_datetime': 'x', 'experiment_index': 'x'} -> Copy names given twice: ['x']
validation {'session_start_datetime': '_tag_x'} -> Copy names use a reserved prefix: ['_tag_x']
validation {'session_start_datetime': 'task_id'} -> Copy names already used: ['task_id']
validation {'task_id': 't'} -> Not tag columns: ['task_id']

